---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Swishtag Platform | Promo Commerce Software";
const description = "Explore Swishtag platforms for PunchOut, artwork approvals, decorator workflows and focused Shopify apps.";
const canonical = "https://cms.swishtag.com/platforms/";
const robots = "index,follow";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} robots={robots}>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/generic-page.css" />
  <main><section class="gp-hero"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-kicker">Platform</div><h1>Software that fills the gaps around your commerce stack.</h1><p>Use focused tools where they remove manual work. Keep the systems that already work, then add a cleaner layer for procurement, artwork, production, and storefront workflows.</p><div class="gp-actions"><a class="gp-btn primary" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a><a class="gp-btn secondary" href="/solutions/">Explore solutions</a></div></div></section><section class="gp-section"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-section-head"><h2>Build around the workflow, not the software list.</h2><p>The strongest architecture is usually the one with fewer handoffs, clear ownership and integrations only where they remove repeated work.</p></div><div class="gp-grid"><article aria-label="Open PunchOut Solutions" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/platforms/punchout-solutions/" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>PROCUREMENT</small><h3>PunchOut Solutions</h3><p>Connect Shopify purchasing experiences with enterprise procurement workflows.</p><a href="/platforms/punchout-solutions/">Explore PunchOut Solutions →</a></article><article aria-label="Open Promo Plus" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/platforms/promo-plus/" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>ARTWORK</small><h3>Promo Plus</h3><p>Centralize artwork approvals, revisions and production-ready files.</p><a href="/platforms/promo-plus/">Explore Promo Plus →</a></article><article aria-label="Open Xecutor" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/platforms/xecutor/" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>PRODUCTION</small><h3>Xecutor</h3><p>Organize decorator production, workstations, inventory and fulfillment.</p><a href="/platforms/xecutor/">Explore Xecutor →</a></article><article aria-label="Open Rocket Apps" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/platforms/shopify-apps-for-promotional-products/" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>SHOPIFY APPS</small><h3>Rocket Apps</h3><p>Add focused Shopify functionality without rebuilding the whole storefront.</p><a href="/platforms/shopify-apps-for-promotional-products/">Explore Rocket Apps →</a></article></div></div></section><section class="gp-section alt"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-split"><div><h2>What this page will cover</h2></div><div class="gp-list"><div>Keep Shopify as the commerce layer when it fits the use case.</div><div>Connect procurement or supplier systems only where the workflow needs it.</div><div>Automate repeated approvals, routing and production handoffs.</div><div>Avoid forcing every business process into one monolithic platform.</div></div></div></div></section><section class="gp-section"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-cta"><div><h2>Have a workflow that does not fit off-the-shelf software?</h2><p>Show us the current process. We can help identify the simplest Shopify, integration, or automation approach before you commit to a larger build.</p></div><a class="gp-btn" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a></div><p class="gp-note">This page is connected and launch-ready. Detailed sales copy, proof, screenshots and SEO depth can be expanded in the next content pass.</p></div></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
